## Summary: Key Design Points

**Frontend:**
- Statements grouped by round, newest round first
- Two vote buttons per statement (Agree/Disagree)
- Green (#2a9d4e) for agree, red (#e00) for disagree
- Button disabled after voting (opacity 0.7)
- Vote counts shown only if > 0
- Badge shows unvoted count on Statements tab

**Backend:**
- Votes stored as `Dict[participant_id -> vote_string]` in Statement.votes
- No re-voting (checked in `record_vote()`)
- All participants see their own vote state and aggregate counts in real-time
- Mock mode cycles through MOCK_STATEMENTS batches on each analysis trigger
- Analysis triggered every 3 transcript entries
- Round advances when statement count reaches threshold (default 5)

**Mock Testing:**
- Call `POST /api/sessions/{session_id}/mock` repeatedly to inject 3-entry batches
- Automatically triggers analysis which extracts statements from MOCK_STATEMENTS
- Returns: `{added, total, remaining}` for tracking progress
